-- BrandDesk, the production wing of HQ (LOCKED by Sean 2026-11-01: "lock it"). Concept session with V;
-- canon canon-branddesk-production-wing, playbook branddesk-production-wing (brand lesaruss). Records the decision; the build follows.
insert into public.knowledge_records (slug, title, category, subcategory, status, owner, always_load, load_priority, tags, version, created_by, updated_by, change_summary, body)
select 'canon-branddesk-production-wing',
  'BrandDesk: the Studio renamed, HQ''s production wing, wizards rented by Partners on shared 111-day periods (LOCKED by Sean 2026-11-01)',
  'decisions', 'business', 'active', 'sar', false, 40,
  array['lesaruss','branddesk','studio','depot','partner-plan','pricing','periods','vegans-explore'], 1, 'v', 'v',
  'Locked by Sean ("lock it") after a concept session with V.',
  jsonb_build_object(
    'why', 'Sean: "I think we inadvertently created a new depot with the brand desk when it all should just be one thing... I''ve never gone in the studio... if I don''t use, the client''s not going to use it... a very visually appealing, easy, agent-supported place where a client can go in and update their stuff." Then: "maybe brand desk is the rebranding of studio... our proprietary thing that sets us apart."',
    'what', 'BrandDesk is the Studio at hq.lesaruss.ai/studio, renamed and made the product. It lives in HQ. Every brand is a record there (ours, clients'', and any brand set up ad hoc, which is moved in). It replaces the Studio, the Vegans Explore Depot and Depot > BrandDesk. HQ has two wings: BrandDesk, the production wing, and Operations (people, finance, compliance).',
    'foundation', 'The brand kit comes first and is never rushed: from scratch with examples at every step (a mood board tells us style, type and color), or an existing kit plugged in, with anything that could be stronger prompted to the client (self-serve) or the Community Manager. Approved by the client means locked: the kit is the record for everything made after it. A locked part changes only on a request with a reason, approved by the owner, kept on record.',
    'launch_gate', 'No module opens until the kit is locked and the brand launches, our own brands included. Then the brand sees its next steps by what it bought and what we decided it needs.',
    'plan', 'A 3, 6 or 12 month marketing plan rolls out dated tasks backwards from each due date: what to do today, the questions needed to write the article, the photographer to book by a date with the request drafted. Every piece moves the same way: ask, draft, approve or comment, keep working until done, store it.',
    'modules', 'Every module is a best-in-class wizard made the way the Guides were, knowing the business from its locked kit and Library and asking only what it does not know. First: Website and Social (Depot > Social''s plan; everything posted goes through it). As we use them ourselves: Video, YouTube, Podcast, Book, Mobile app, Pitch deck. Product launch is a premium incubator (buyer questions, then a paid review by an approved industry person with honest feedback) listed as Coming with a waitlist; it launches only once we hold the distributor and buyer relationships. A module ships to clients only after we run it on our own brands.',
    'library_and_results', 'Everything a module makes goes into the brand''s Library on its own. Analytics live inside BrandDesk per brand; Reports roll it up per brand and across brands.',
    'support', 'Same screens for everyone, chosen per wizard: Self-serve (an agent for questions), Supported (an agent drafts and pushes, the client approves), Managed (a Community Manager works with the agent and our automated processes, the client approves). The owner can invite their own people. The managed service already built ($1,500 setup, $500 a month) is Managed, bundled.',
    'the_standard', 'What works for us is the standard; every lesson updates the standard and its wizards for every brand.',
    'pricing', 'BrandDesk is a perk of the $111 Partner plan, the door. Wizards are rented on top, never owned: by the month, the period or the year, each priced on its own; buy when ready to produce, renew past the period. Each squeeze page shows what the wizard has produced (mostly our own brands). Buying a wizard from its squeeze page makes the buyer a Partner. A lapsed rental closes the wizard; finished work stays in the Library while they are a Partner. Leaving the plan: 30 days to download everything they made.',
    'periods', 'A period is 111 days, called a period, never a quarter ("$111 a period", "every 111 days"). Everyone is on one calendar, back to back across year-end, no pauses: Period 1 Jan 1 to Apr 21, 2027; 2 Apr 22 to Aug 10; 3 Aug 11 to Nov 29; 4 Nov 30, 2027 to Mar 19, 2028; and on.',
    'joining', 'The door never closes. Days 1 to 90: pay a prorated share of the days left, start at once, renew with everyone at the next period. Days 91 to 111, the Preparation window: pay the full $111 for the next period; the 21 days are the preparation cycle, building and locking the brand kit so they start day 1 with modules open. Preparation windows: Dec 11 to 31, 2026; Apr 1 to 21, 2027; Jul 21 to Aug 10; Nov 9 to 29. Promotion opens about two weeks before each window and peaks in it. Nothing runs as a cohort; past hot labs stay open.',
    'front_row_start', 'Front Row Start changes: they pay now. The first $111 is charged at sign-up and buys Period 1 (from Jan 1, 2027); every day before then is bonus (Sean: "I''m not going to wait to get paid until January"). The early Partners'' equity is their feedback. Anyone already on the old no-charge trial keeps the terms they were given.',
    'retreat', 'Idea for later, not a commitment: a member retreat in a Preparation window, finishing members and new ones together.',
    'build_order', '1. The Partner checkout (money first): $111 or a prorated share at sign-up, the Preparation window, renewals on the shared calendar, "period" wording everywhere. 2. Rename the Studio to BrandDesk in HQ (/studio redirects); each brand''s page its home. 3. The foundation: brand kit with mood board, lock and launch gate. 4. Social and Website modules. 5. The plan engine. 6. Run it on Sean A. Russell, GeekFon Society and Vegans Explore, then Green Leaf Kitchen as the demo, then the first client; Pitch deck the first new wizard. The Depot''s pages keep working until each has a home; nothing is cut until a usage log shows it unused.',
    'playbook', 'branddesk-production-wing')
where not exists (select 1 from public.knowledge_records where slug = 'canon-branddesk-production-wing');

insert into public.playbook_records (slug, brand_slug, author, body, source, kind)
select 'branddesk-production-wing', 'lesaruss', 'V',
  'Locked by Sean 2026-11-01 ("lock it"). BrandDesk is the Studio renamed: HQ''s production wing, replacing the Studio and the Vegans Explore Depot. Brand kit first, approved means locked, launch gate before any module. Modules are wizards (Website and Social first; Video, YouTube, Podcast, Book, Mobile app, Pitch deck as we use them; Product launch premium, waiting on distributor relationships). A marketing plan rolls out dated tasks; every piece is ask, draft, approve, store. Library, Analytics and Reports per brand. Support per wizard: Self-serve, Supported, Managed. Pricing: BrandDesk is a perk of the $111 Partner plan; wizards rented by month, period or year. Periods are 111 days on one shared calendar from Jan 1, 2027; join days 1 to 90 prorated, days 91 to 111 is the Preparation window at full price (brand kit preparation). Front Row Start now pays at sign-up, days before Jan 1 bonus. Build order: Partner checkout, rename the Studio, the foundation, Social and Website, the plan engine, our brands first. Full record: canon canon-branddesk-production-wing; proposal docs/proposals/depot-one-desk.md in lesaruss/vegansexplore-com.',
  'text', 'decision'
where not exists (select 1 from public.playbook_records where slug = 'branddesk-production-wing' and kind = 'decision');
